UID:bloomberg-green-docs-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174936Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
SUMMARY:Deadline: Bloomberg Green Docs Competition 2026 (Short Climate Docu
 mentary)
DESCRIPTION:The Bloomberg Green Docs competition is open to all eligible fi
 lmmakers competing for a $25\,000 grand prize for a short climate document
 ary. The call seeks films that explore our climate future and reveal the w
 orld we are making today: ecosystems being restored\, tomorrow's zero-carb
 on communities being formed\, and habitat extremes warning of cascading cl
 imate consequences. REQUIREMENTS: films must address the urgency of climat
 e change and run under 10 minutes including credits. The jury awards a $25
 \,000 grand prize\, announced at the Bloomberg Green Docs Film Festival in
  New York City on 22 September 2026\, where the top five documentaries wil
 l be screened. Check the official rules on the competition site for eligib
 ility details. DEADLINE: submissions accepted through 14 August 2026.\n\nO
 rganisation: Bloomberg Green\nLocation: Open call for filmmakers (see elig
 ibility rules on the site)\; festival screening in New York City\, USA.\nA
 ward: $25\,000 grand prize awarded by a jury\; the top five documentaries 
 screen at the Bloomberg Green Docs Film Festival in New York City. No entr
 y fee stated.\nDuration: Winner announced at the festival on 22 September 
 2026\n\nMore: https://www.bloomberg.com/greendocs/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bloomberg.com/greendocs/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open call for filmmakers (see eligibility rules on the site)\; fes
 tival screening in New York City\, USA.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:new-emergence-art-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174936Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: New Emergence Art Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:The New Emergence Art Prize 2026 is an international open call 
 for emerging artists\, presented by New Emergence Art. There is no set the
 me and work may be submitted in any medium. AWARDS: a prize fund worth ove
 r GBP 5\,000 across nine awards supporting artists through cash prizes\, a
 rtist materials\, mentoring\, and a residency\, including a GBP 1\,000 Gra
 nd Prize\, a two-week NG Art Creative Residency in Provence\, France (wort
 h EUR 2\,000)\, a GBP 300 Founder's Prize cash award\, and materials or su
 bscription awards from Staedtler UK\, Rosemary & Co\, GreatArt\, Michael H
 arding\, and The Art Ladder. ELIGIBILITY: open internationally to emerging
  artists\; entrants may submit up to three original artworks that represen
 t the quality\, originality and direction of their practice. Final selecti
 ons are made by an independent judging panel considering concept\, executi
 on\, originality and impact. Shortlisted artists are featured in an online
  exhibition running 11 August to 7 September 2026. NOTE: there is a paid e
 ntry fee (amount set at the entry step). DEADLINE: 3 August 2026\, 23:59 B
 ST. Apply via https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply.\n\nOrganisation: New 
 Emergence Art\nLocation: International\; open worldwide. Shortlist shown i
 n an online exhibition.\nAward: Prize fund worth over GBP 5\,000 across ni
 ne awards\, including a GBP 1\,000 Grand Prize cash award\, a two-week NG 
 Art Creative Residency in Provence\, France (worth EUR 2\,000)\, a GBP 300
  Founder's Prize cash award\, and materials or subscription awards from St
 aedtler UK\, Rosemary & Co\, GreatArt\, Michael Harding\, and The Art Ladd
 er. NOTE: there is a paid entry fee.\nDuration: One-off prize\; shortliste
 d artists shown in an online exhibition 11 August to 7 September 2026\n\nM
 ore: https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.newemergenceart.com/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International\; open worldwide. Shortlist shown in an online exhib
 ition.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:berggruen-prize-essay-competition-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174936Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: Berggruen Prize Essay Competition 2026: A New Axial Age?
DESCRIPTION:Annual essay competition from the Berggruen Institute\, a compa
 nion to the Berggruen Prize for Philosophy & Culture\, seeking new thinkin
 g and cross-cultural perspectives on fundamental philosophical questions o
 f significance for contemporary life and the future. It looks for essays i
 n the tradition of Rousseau\, Montaigne\, and Emerson (models cited includ
 e Frankfurt\, Nagel\, Sontag\, Fukuyama\, and recent Noema pieces)\, not p
 eer-reviewed academic work: novel ideas\, clearly argued in compelling way
 s for intellectually serious readers. THEME for 2026: 'A New Axial Age?' R
 eferencing Karl Jaspers's Axial Age (c. 800-200 BCE)\, the prompt asks whe
 ther civilisation is again at a 'hinge of history' undergoing a pivotal tr
 ansformation of consciousness driven by rapid technological change and its
  social\, economic\, and political consequences. Suggested (non-exhaustive
 ) angles: the foundational ideas and institutions underpinning present and
  future societies\; the philosophical implications of the current era\; th
 e future of human evolution and life amid the ecological crisis\; shared c
 onceptual foundations for a common future\; global transformation driven b
 y technology and the rise of AI\; the end of the global order and its rami
 fications\; and the future of life amid biotechnology and synthetic life. 
 Entrants may choose their own topic\; for 2026 creative fiction is accepte
 d. ELIGIBILITY: open to the public\; not for academic papers and not gover
 ned by academic disciplinary standards or affiliations. Length up to 10\,0
 00 words in English or 15\,000 characters in Chinese (excluding diagrams\,
  tables\, endnotes\, bibliography\, or authorship declaration). One submis
 sion per year per entrant\, in either English or Chinese\; co-authorship a
 llowed. Submissions must be original and previously unpublished. AI USAGE:
  generative AI must not be used to create content or substitute original t
 hought\, and entrants must engage primary sources rather than AI summaries
 \; AI is permitted only for proofreading/grammar\, as quoted supporting ma
 terial when AI itself is the subject of the research\, or for translating 
 an essay into English or Chinese\, and all AI use (including AI-assisted t
 ranslation) must be disclosed on the front page or the entry is disqualifi
 ed. JUDGING: originality\, clarity\, and style. Essays are due by 23:59 PT
  on 17 August 2026\; PDF only. Chinese-language submissions use a separate
  page. Inquiries to essay@berggruen.org.\n\nOrganisation: Berggruen Instit
 ute\nLocation: Remote/online\; open to the public worldwide (English and C
 hinese submissions)\nAward: USD 50\,000 for the winning English essay and 
 USD 50\,000 for the winning Chinese essay. If there is more than one winne
 r in a language category\, the prize is split evenly. Winning essays are p
 ublished through BI Press or Noema. No entry fee.\nDuration: One-off compe
 tition\; submissions open 17 March 2026 and close 17 August 2026\n\nMore: 
 https://berggruen.org/eu/essay-competition-open?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://berggruen.org/eu/essay-competition-open?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote/online\; open to the public worldwide (English and Chinese 
 submissions)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amr-paper-of-the-future-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174936Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: AMR: 2026 Paper of the Future Prize
DESCRIPTION:USD 10\,000 prize from the Association for Mathematical Researc
 h for serious experimentation in how mathematicians communicate with one a
 nother\, beyond the static PDF. Submissions should demonstrate communicati
 ve capabilities fundamentally unavailable in a linear paper: interactive e
 xploration of parameter spaces in differential equations\, dynamic visuali
 sation of group actions or geometric structures\, multi-perspective repres
 entations of algebraic or number-theoretic objects\, nonlinear navigation 
 of proof architectures or dependency graphs\, embedded computation as part
  of exposition\, or similar. ELIGIBILITY: no nationality\, institutional o
 r career restriction stated\; the focus is mathematical depth and communic
 ative innovation. This is NOT for popularisation\, production polish or sh
 ort-form video content - it is about novel research-to-research communicat
 ion. EVALUATION CRITERIA: mathematical depth and rigor\; conceptual insigh
 t enabled by the medium\; communicative innovation beyond static expositio
 n\; scalability and reproducibility\; transformative potential for researc
 h communication. PROCESS: initial submissions are a short public YouTube c
 oncept demonstration (with the hashtag #AMRPotF and a concise written expl
 anation of the mathematical substance and communicative innovation in the 
 video description)\, with the YouTube link emailed to PotFPrize@amathr.org
 . Finalists are asked to provide a fully accessible prototype suitable for
  hosting or linking within AMR Reviews\; the winning submission will be pu
 blished in AMR Reviews as an interactive exposition. Selection committee: 
 Mohammed Abouzaid\, Benson Farb\, Alex Kontorovich\, Akshay Venkatesh\, Ma
 ryna Viazovska.\n\nOrganisation: Association for Mathematical Research (AM
 R)\nLocation: Worldwide (digital submission)\nAward: USD 10\,000 prize to 
 the winner\; runner-up recognitions at committee discretion. The committee
  reserves the right to withhold the prize if no submissions meet the stand
 ards.\nDuration: Project-based\n\nMore: https://amathr.org/prizes/paper-of
 -the-future-prize-prize/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://amathr.org/prizes/paper-of-the-future-prize-prize/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide (digital submission)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day-job-short-film-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174936Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: Day Job: Short Film Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:Short film competition from Day Job Films created to give auteu
 r directors full creative freedom\, awarding a production budget of up to 
 GBP 7\,000 to make a short film with no producer interference or commercia
 l agenda. Open to animation\, live-action and documentary projects. Runs i
 n three rounds: (1) a pitch deck outlining concept\, story\, key character
 s and visual style\; (2) a full script for those who progress\; and (3) an
  interview to discuss the vision and execution. A panel of industry profes
 sionals judges the pitch deck\, script and interview\, with at least one t
 eam member reading each pitch deck and script in full. The winner receives
  full creative control over the project. ELIGIBILITY: applicants can be fr
 om anywhere worldwide\, but all production must take place in the UK\; app
 licants must have a producer on board who is separate from the director/wr
 iter. Applicants may optionally include a plan for adapting the script int
 o a feature-length film (this does not affect the outcome). Submissions op
 en February 10\, 2026 and close August 10\, 2026. Enquiries: hello@dayjobf
 ilms.com.\n\nOrganisation: Day Job Films\nLocation: Worldwide applicants\;
  all production must take place in the UK\nAward: Production budget of up 
 to GBP 7\,000\, with full creative control and no producer or external int
 erference. No application fee.\nDuration: Per short film project\n\nMore: 
 https://www.dayjobfilms.com/short-film-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.dayjobfilms.com/short-film-fund?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide applicants\; all production must take place in the UK
END:VEVENT
